{"seq":1,"slug":"sets-logic","title":"集合与逻辑","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/high-school/year-1/mathematics/sets-logic","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"set-theory","title":"高一数学 — 集合论","url":"/l-doc-books/education/high-school/year-1/mathematics/sets-logic/set-theory","wordCount":1734,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"logical-connectives","title":"高一数学 — 逻辑联结词","url":"/l-doc-books/education/high-school/year-1/mathematics/sets-logic/logical-connectives","wordCount":1580,"readingTime":7},{"seq":3,"slug":"sufficient-necessary","title":"高一数学 — 充分必要条件","url":"/l-doc-books/education/high-school/year-1/mathematics/sets-logic/sufficient-necessary","wordCount":1712,"readingTime":7}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"集合与逻辑-简介\">集合与逻辑 简介</h1><p>本章是高一数学的开篇内容，引入集合和逻辑这两个贯穿整个高中数学的基础工具。集合提供了描述数学对象的规范语言，逻辑则提供了判断命题真假和进行推理论证的方法。掌握这些内容，是准确理解函数定义域、不等式解集、方程解集等后续概念的前提。</p>\n<p>本章包含三个小节。<strong>集合理论基础</strong>从集合的概念和元素的确定性、互异性、无序性三大特征讲起，涵盖集合的列举法与描述法表示、子集与真子集的关系判断、交集并集补集三种运算，以及 Venn 图的直观表示方法，建立用集合语言描述数学问题的基本能力。<strong>逻辑联结词</strong>讲解&quot;且&quot;&quot;或&quot;&quot;非&quot;三种逻辑运算在数学命题中的含义与用法，训练学生准确理解复合命题的结构，并能判断复合命题的真假，这是正确进行数学推理的关键环节。<strong>充分条件与必要条件</strong>是高中逻辑推理的核心概念，本节通过大量实例辨析&quot;如果 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span></span></span></span></span> 则 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span></span></span></span></span>&quot;中 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span></span></span></span></span> 与 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span></span></span></span></span> 的逻辑关系，讲解充分不必要、必要不充分、充要、既不充分也不必要四种情形的判断方法。</p>\n<p>建议按顺序学习。集合是逻辑的载体，逻辑联结词是充要条件判断的基础。学习时注意从具体数值集合入手建立直觉，再逐步过渡到抽象命题的推理，同时多做条件关系的判断练习以巩固理解。</p>\n"}